documents this failure mode): a single stray #text node - a ~106-line blob of duplicated comment prose that
had leaked OUTSIDE the comment delimiters - sat directly under <Project>. MSBuild therefore rejected the
project with MSB4067 ("element <#text> beneath element <Project> is unrecognized"), so the ENTIRE solution
build/test was red before any WidgetShell work (verified: bare baseline dotnet build apps/windows/TeslaSync.sln
failed with MSB4067; git status showed the file unmodified vs HEAD). Per the file's own documented remedy
("when that happens, regenerate it directly from the ... sources on disk"), the single stray text node was
surgically removed - exactly ONE Project root, ONE PropertyGroup, FOUR ItemGroups and ALL 1308 existing
Compile links preserved - and the 3 WidgetShell Microsoft.UI-free Compile links (Model / Source / ViewModel;
the WinUI view WidgetShell.cs is excluded and exercised by the app build) were added. Diff: 1 file, +4 / -106.
Post-repair the project loads (no MSB4067 / MSB4025) and the full solution builds (BUILD below).

